d1a1/opencode)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": false, "main_agent_searched": true, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "output_tail": " (not applied):**\n1. Rename `\"rat\"` to `\"fee_rate\"` in `settings.json`.\n2. Change `main.py` to fail with a clear error when the key is missing, instead of using 0.\n\n**Other things it noticed:**\n- Code reads config in different ways: some files read the settings directly, others call `get_setting()`.\n- `csv_writer.py` builds the key as `\"fee_\" + \"rate\"`, so searching for `fee_rate` won't find it.\n- After the fix, the total prints as `5.0`, which may need formatting as currency.\n\nWant me to apply one or both fixes?\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: bash]\nI checked the subagent's findings myself. Three places read the setting. Fixing the key in `settings.json` covers all of them.\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: bash]\nI fixed the bug by renaming the key in `settings.json:2` from `\"rat\"` to `\"fee_rate\"`. All three places that read the setting now work.\n\n**Every place that reads the setting:**\n\n| File:line | How it reads it | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `main.py:11` | `cfg[\"fee_rate\"]`, falls back to 0 if missing | `Total: 0` | `Total: 5.0` |\n| `billing/report.py:7` | `get_setting(\"fee_rate\")` | exited with \"fee_rate is missing\" | `Report fee: 0.5` |\n| `billing/export/csv_writer.py:8` | `settings.get(\"fee_\" + \"rate\")` | exited with \"fee_rate is missing\" | `CSV fee: 0.5` |\n\nI ran all three before and after the change; those are the outputs above. Nothing read the old `\"rat\"` key, so renaming it doesn't break anything.\n\n**Things that look like the setting but don't read it:**\n- `billing/invoice.py:5` only uses `\"fee_rate\"` as a column name.\n- `billing/discount.py:5` has its own fixed rate of 0.15.\n- `billing/tax.py:4-5` uses fixed tax rates.\n- `billing/audit.py:4` builds `\"fee_code\u2026\"` strings.\n- `app/config.py:15` is the `get_setting()` helper that loads the settings, so it doesn't read this key itself.\n\nI left `main.py` as it is, so it still quietly uses a rate of 0 if the key is ever missing again. Want me to make it fail with an error like the other two scripts?", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 5, "replies_ok": null, "replies_throttled": null, "requests_cache_read": 131067, "requests_cache_write": 36448, "requests_cost_usd": 0.3065734, "requests_count": 14, "requests_input_uncached": 1580, "requests_output": 4590, "reread": true, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "opencode:trig-subagent-followup:claude-opus-5-5:trial18", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 69, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-18T05:19:31.867168+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 1, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 54.561, "t_checker_s": 0.226, "t_env_setup_s": 0.007, "task": "trig-subagent-followup", "task_calls": 1, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 840, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "estimated", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 6170, "tokens_cache_read": 131067, "tokens_cache_write": 36448, "tokens_fresh": 2679, "tokens_input_uncached": 1580, "tokens_main_cache_read": 107864, "tokens_main_cache_write": 15510, "tokens_main_calls": 7, "tokens_main_input_uncached": 18, "tokens_main_output": 2661, "tokens_output": 4590, "tokens_proxy_cache_read": 131067, "tokens_proxy_cache_write": 36448, "tokens_proxy_calls": 14, "tokens_proxy_input_uncached": 1580, "tokens_proxy_output": 4590, "tokens_proxy_reasoning": null, "tokens_reasoning": 0, "toolchain"